WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:04.740
It turns out that Avengers: Endgame's writers
don't simply have a soft spot for deadly,

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:05.740
green alien warriors.

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:10.320
In a recent interview with CinemaBlend, Christopher
Markus and Stephen McFeely revealed that they

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:14.860
had a specific reason for including the return
of Gamora in their script: so the character

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:18.700
would be available for James Gunn to use in
the upcoming Guardians of the Galaxy Vol.

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:19.200
3.

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:23.000
You'll recall that of the many, many shocking
deaths to be featured in Avengers: Infinity

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:26.300
War, Gamora's was one that seemed as if it
would be permanent.

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:31.260
She was forced to accompany her adoptive father
Thanos to the planet Vormir, where anyone

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:35.160
brave and/or determined enough could acquire
the Soul Stone... for a price.

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:39.320
Thanos was informed by the stone's protector
that in order to possess the stone, one must

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:41.980
give up that which what they love — and
it just so happened the only thing Thanos

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:45.740
loved in the universe, his daughter, was standing
right next to him.

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:49.230
"I ignored my destiny once.

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:51.740
I cannot do that again.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:55.600
Even… for you.”

00:00:56.080 --> 00:01:00.800
Thanos hesitated for the briefest of moments
before chucking Gamora to her doom from one

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:05.030
of Vormir's rocky cliffs, securing the stone
and eventually succeeding in his mission to

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:08.030
snap half of all life in the universe out
of existence.

00:01:08.030 --> 00:01:12.140
Gamora, however like Loki and Heimdall, who
met their ends in the film's brutal opening

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:15.780
scene didn't perish in the Snap, but was killed
outright by Thanos.

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:19.979
Also, her death was the price for securing
the Soul Stone... and as we learned when Black

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:24.340
Widow sacrificed herself so that Hawkeye could
get his hands on that very stone during the

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:27.960
events of Avengers: Endgame, such a death
cannot be reversed.

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:32.640
Markus and McFeely, however, found a way around
that problem by using the Avengers' time-traveling

00:01:32.649 --> 00:01:37.880
Endgame shenanigans to re-introduce the 2014
version of Gamora, one who had not yet met

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:38.640
up with the Guardians.

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:43.280
In the scribes' conversation with CinemaBlend,
McFeely clarified that that particular plot

00:01:43.291 --> 00:01:47.280
element was basically put in place so that
Gunn could have his entire team on deck for

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:48.140
Guardians 3.

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:48.880
He explained:

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:53.100
"There are... parts [in Endgame that were
written] so that Gunn could do whatever he

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:53.640
needs to do."

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:58.960
McFeely also referenced that poignant Endgame
deleted scene that made it clear that 2014

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:01.499
Gamora wanted nothing further to do with anyone.

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:02.040
He said:

00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:05.560
"You saw the behind the scenes stuff where
they all kneel, and [Gamora] sort of boogies

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:06.200
off set.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:10.140
If [the filmmakers had left that scene in],
you would've gone, 'Oh, she's alive and she's

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:10.680
over there.'

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:12.000
It's very vague now.

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:13.740
I don't know what [Gunn is] going to do with
it."

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:17.640
Well, neither do we, but that's never stopped
us from speculating.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:22.640
2014 Gamora pointedly does not take off with
the Guardians at the conclusion of Endgame,

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:23.960
and really, why would she?

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:26.320
She has no idea who these people even are.

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:27.740
Where could she be heading off to?

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:32.300
Parts unknown, obviously... but with her adoptive
father gone and her relationship with Peter

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:36.860
Quill never having been forged, there's really
only one person in the galaxy she has any

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:41.880
kind of kinship with — her sister, Nebula,
who is currently tagging along with the Guardians.

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:44.660
"You should fight one another for the honor
of leadership."

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:46.000
"Sounds fair."

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.820
"Well I — that's not necessary."

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:50.480
"It's not."

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:54.780
Perhaps Gamora will seek out Nebula in an
attempt to get some answers about what in

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:59.290
hell exactly happened with Thanos and the
weird army of superpowered Terrans, or maybe

00:02:59.290 --> 00:03:03.650
she'll head off into some forbidding corner
of the galaxy and get herself into a jam — the

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:07.400
kind of jam that her friends would be compelled
to help bail her out of, even if she doesn't

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:08.420
exactly know them yet.

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:12.750
It's worth noting that Gunn wasn't blindsided
by Gamora's fate in Infinity War, but was

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:16.700
totally in the loop as to what Markus and
McFeely intended to do with his character

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:20.420
— meaning that he's had plenty of time to
mull over where to take her arc in Guardians

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:20.960
3.

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:24.880
It would absolutely shock us if the "deadliest
woman in the galaxy" was anything but key

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:29.000
to the plot of the third Guardians movie — heck,
perhaps she'll even somehow find a way to

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:33.800
rediscover the memories of her alternate timeline
self, the one who died so that her "father"

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:35.640
might succeed in his terrible mission.

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:40.040
It would take some pretty hardcore narrative
acrobatics, but if anyone is capable of pulling

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:43.360
those off without shattering our suspension
of disbelief, it's Gunn.

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:47.960
In any event, the situation interestingly
illustrates the kind of synergy necessary

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:52.300
for all of these amazing franchises to exist
within the same shared universe, and — as

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:56.940
McFeely noted — the extent to which filmmakers
must be content to simply pass the ball to

00:03:56.940 --> 00:03:59.980
the next person to continue the story of any
given character.

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:01.040
McFeely said:

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:04.000
"I... liked that little dangling piece of
time travel.

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:07.850
The bow wasn't completely wrapped up and there
was a little bit of an after effect...

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:12.160
I don't know how it's going to affect the
coming Guardians, but just leaving some strings,

00:04:12.260 --> 00:04:16.360
when you're tying up this many strings, it's
satisfying to know that there are a few still

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:16.900
dangling."

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:21.260
For as long as the Marvel Cinematic Universe
exists — that is to say, until the Earth

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:25.250
is actually swallowed up by Galactus — it
seems likely that there will always be a few

00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:27.800
strings left for the next filmmaker in line
to tug on.

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:31.820
As far as this one goes, we're going to go
ahead and guess that Guardians 3 will see

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:36.220
Quill remember his way to Gamora's heart:
through the musical stylings of Elvin Bishop.

00:04:36.820 --> 00:04:38.220
His melodies are pleasant.

